     line) and DlrRun.Closure/Machine(..., file, line) are gone. A consumer built against rc.2 must be
     rebuilt. Old-signature forwarders were tried and do not work: an rc.2 consumer's stored
     quotations decode against the new Delay as invalid nodes, and an old Delay overload would win
     overload resolution for new code. Nothing else may be added here without a decision like that
     one; drop these once the baseline moves past 1.0.0-rc.2. -->
